.TH CVECTOR_DESTROY 3 "2026-09-28" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cvector_destroy \- destroy a vector and set pointer to NULL
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

cvector_destroy(v)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Frees every resource of the vector, the data buffer included. The
function then sets the vector pointer to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v    Vector to destroy. It must be a modifiable lvalue, such as a
     variable or an element of an array. The macro evaluates it exactly
     once, and sets it to NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Safe to call with a NULL pointer (a no-op)
Does not free the elements one by one. A vector can hold pointers to
heap buffers. The caller must free that element data first when it is
necessary
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvector_create (3)
